11.6.3. RestTemplate
Spring Framework’s RestTemplate class predates RestClient and is the classic way that many
applications use to call remote REST services. You might choose to use RestTemplate when you have
existing code that you don’t want to migrate to RestClient, or because you’re already familiar with
the RestTemplate API.
Since RestTemplate instances often need to be customized before being used, Spring Boot does not
provide any single auto-configured RestTemplate bean. It does, however, auto-configure a
RestTemplateBuilder, which can be used to create RestTemplate instances when needed.

